{
  "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The composition is a 3/4 overhead view at a 40-degree angle, centered perfectly in the frame with generous negative space for cropping, ensuring the entire dish is visible. The scene features two matte ceramic plates set on an aged oak table with a visible wood grain. In the primary sharp plate, a golden-brown, pan-seared rainbow trout fillet with a crisp, slightly irregular skin texture rests next to a vibrant bed of quinoa, bright green peas, and just-wilted dark green baby spinach. The quinoa has a light coating of Dijon-lemon dressing that glistens under soft, natural window light from the left. A second plate is visible but softly blurred in the background. Props include a small ramekin with extra chopped fresh dill and a stainless steel fork resting on a rumpled linen napkin beside the plate. The trout shows a tender, pearly white, flaky interior. A few stray peas and a small green dill sprig are scattered naturally on the table surface. Soft, natural side lighting creates gentle shadows and highlights the moisture of the pan juices. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene reflects a home-cooked, warm, and authentic atmosphere. Small, realistic imperfections like a tiny sauce drip on the rim, uneven browning on the trout, and slight organic scattering of the greens. No plastic sheen, no unnatural smoothness. Warm, golden-hour color temperature. No text, watermarks, hands, or faces. Indistinguishable from professional cookbook photography."
}
